# Rust / Cargo build output
/target
**/*.rs.bk

# Our own build artifacts (objects, linked kernel, ISO, isofiles staging)
/build

# Kernel image staged into the web tutorial (produced by `make web`)
/web/kernel.bin
# Staged for the browser tutorial by `make web` (reproducible; not committed —
# no page fetches it; qemu-wasm packs its own FS)
/web/ziran.iso

# NOTE: the other web runtime assets (vendor/, libv86.js, v86.wasm, seabios.bin,
# vgabios.bin, kernel-v86.bin, out.js, load.js, qemu-system-x86_64.*) ARE tracked,
# deliberately: the Pages project deploys from git, so anything a page fetches must
# be committed or production 404s it (see docs/DEPLOY.md). All are under Pages'
# 25 MiB per-file cap. `web/kernel-v86.bin` is a build artifact — re-stage it with
# `make stage-web-kernel` and commit it whenever the kernel changes.

# Tier-2 CTF exploit recipe (kept out of the public repo so the live challenge
# isn't pre-solved for a reader/scraper; the *concept* stays public, the concrete
# per-session recipe does not). Author's private operational note.
/ctf-server/*.private.md

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Claude Code local worktrees (transient; never publish)
.claude/worktrees/

# wrangler local state (dropped by `npx wrangler` runs)
.wrangler/
